---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Start here — the Audit or the Blueprint | Panta"
  description="One standard for a digital presence that works, two ways in: the Audit finds the leaks in an existing presence; the Blueprint is the build plan when you're starting fresh."
>
  <section class="section section--dark hero" style="padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem);">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label">Start here</p>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.4rem);">One standard. Two ways in.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        We hold every digital presence to the same 40-check standard — can
        people find you, trust you, and choose you? Where you start depends on
        what exists today.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid--2" style="align-items: stretch;">
        <div class="card" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; padding: 2.25rem;">
          <p class="label" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Door one · You have a presence</p>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem;">The Digital Presence Audit</h2>
          <p>
            We grade everything you have against the standard, find where
            customers or donors are leaking away, and hand you a prioritized
            90-day fix list — honest about what you can do yourself.
          </p>
          <ul class="checklist" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
            <li>Every channel scored: Visibility · Trust · Conversion · Systems</li>
            <li>Your Top 3 Money Leaks, with what each costs per month</li>
            <li>Baseline metrics, so improvement gets measured</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top: auto;">
            <a href="/audit/" class="btn btn--primary">Explore the Audit</a>
            <span class="small">$950 · founding $750</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; padding: 2.25rem;">
          <p class="label" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Door two · You're starting fresh</p>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem;">The Digital Presence Blueprint</h2>
          <p>
            Nothing to audit yet? We hand you the standard as a build plan:
            which channels matter for your audience, in what order, and what
            "done right" looks like for each — before you spend a dollar
            building the wrong thing.
          </p>
          <ul class="checklist" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
            <li>Fragment scan — what already exists that you don't control</li>
            <li>A 90-day launch sequence, step by step</li>
            <li>Measurement wired from day one — never fly blind</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top: auto;">
            <a href="/blueprint/" class="btn btn--primary">Explore the Blueprint</a>
            <span class="small">$750 · founding $600</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="small" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        Nonprofits get 15% off either door, always.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label">Either way</p>
      <h2>The parts that never change.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top: 2rem; gap: 2rem;">
        <div>
          <h3>10 business days, flat price</h3>
          <p>
            Fixed scope, fixed cost, a 60-minute walkthrough at the end. The
            report is yours whatever you decide next.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>A third of it is free advice</h3>
          <p>
            Every roadmap item is tagged DIY (with a guide) or Project (worth
            hiring out). The honesty is how you know the rest is worth paying
            for.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Re-scored at 90 days, free</h3>
          <p>
            We measure against the same standard three months later — so
            "better" is a number, not a feeling.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label">Not sure which door?</p>
      <h2>Most people aren't. That's our job, not yours.</h2>
      <p>
        Almost nobody is truly at zero — most "new" businesses already have an
        auto-generated Google listing or a directory page they've never seen.
        And some established presences are broken enough that starting from the
        blueprint beats patching. One 20-minute call and a short questionnaire
        route you to the right door; you never have to self-diagnose.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn--primary">Book a free 20-minute call</a>
        <span class="small">We'll tell you which door — even if the answer is "neither yet."</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
